A||N||7||85Josh||Door panel/mirror control bulges||||1||
Z||000000||85Josh||03-25-2001||03:14 PM||||The drivers mirror control on my non-power mirror is pulling away from the door panel, and looks like a**. Anybody got a solution? TIA<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||03-25-2001||03:30 PM||||Someone makes a plate that goes under the panel to straighten it out, search the forum there's more info on it.  Also, I've heard you can use some big washers under the mounting nuts to do the same thing.<BR>Welcome and good luck!<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000002||RacinRob||03-25-2001||03:57 PM||||I just put the big washers on the bottom and that seems to be working for me. I did that last fall and it is still holding up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||85Josh||03-25-2001||04:00 PM||||Thanks, Cozmo, I found this link in the archives: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-000348.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-000348.html</A> <BR>It seems to confirm what RacinRob says. Apreciate the replies, guys1||||reg||1
Z||000004||DavidHenshaw||03-25-2001||06:45 PM||||I made my own plate out of thin stock sheet metal but it wasn't easy. My recommendation, unless you want to try making your own is buy the one mentioned already in one of the above posts. One thing I do know, the plate corrects the problem!<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||03-26-2001||01:49 AM||||Super glue and a plastic credit card!! Yes that is what I used, or was it a phone card??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It works. The super glue makes the door panel board hard, glue the card in place clamp it down so it will stay flat and straight then cut it out and make the holes to mount the control.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000006||TheFiero64||03-26-2001||05:47 PM||||I just used washers on Jaygee79's 84. It seems to be working so far.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||85Josh||03-26-2001||06:18 PM||||DXR_DAD, that's one way to cut down on spending! If it ever warms up (17 degrees in Kentucky today!) I'll try at least one of these ideas.||||reg||1
